course: dictionary
lesson: 11708
title: Short forms: Aug
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shortened so they fit in small spaces. On a calendar or a form, you may see «Aug» instead of August. This short written form is called an abbreviation.
explain: Abbreviations are written, not spoken. When you read «Aug», say "August" out loud. The short form and the full word mean the same month.
explain: Use the context to check. «The school trip is on 5 Aug.» The sentence is about a date, so Aug must mean the month of August. Swap "August" into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Aug is short for August, the eighth month of the year.
fact: «Aug» is an abbreviation: it is written, not spoken. You still say "August".
fact: In a calendar problem, August has 31 days and comes between July and September.
fact: Other months are shortened in the same way: «Jan» for January, «Feb» for February, and «Sep» for September.
fact: In a few technical names, aug can stand for "augmented", but you will meet this rarely.
exercise: On a form, «Aug» is written in the date box. Which month does it stand for? | June | March | October | *August
exercise: Which month comes just before «Aug» on a calendar? | September | June | April | *July
exercise: A timetable says «Trip: 5 Aug». What does Aug mean here? | A day of the week | *The month of August | A type of bus | A maths word for adding
test: Ella sees the label «Aug 3». How should she say it out loud? | Skip it because it is not a word | Say "aug" like a short word | Say "Ah-goo" | *Say "August"
test: Which month, written as «Aug», is the eighth month of the year? | September | *August | April | July
exam: On a school calendar, which abbreviation comes just after «Aug»? | Oct | *Sep | Jul | Jun
